WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Let me just tell you what's going on. You have it?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Which pages?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:18.000
You have about less than an hour to study. It's my fault, I know, because I should have been here earlier, but...

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Take a long time.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Alright. Now, just let me tell you what's going on here.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:43.400
People who are literate, who went to school, went to college, went to university, and then they read the Tora, they read the Bible, in English or Latin, whatever your language happens to be.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.720
And then you see the Bible, and then you see what the law, the halakha requires of you.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.860
And there is a discrepancy.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.080
The Bible seems to be very simple.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.660
Don't work on the Shabbat.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.660
So people don't say don't work on the Shabbat, don't go to your office, or whatever it is.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.660
All of a sudden you strike a match, or you put on a line, or you, I don't know, you sign your initials,

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.660
and all of a sudden they say, ah, that's haram because you work on Shabbat. It doesn't make any sense.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:19.660
So, the problem with Judaism, and this is, that's why you see here the greatness of this haqqaf,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:36.580
The problem with Judaism is not the Bible. Even Christians, even Muslims respect the Bible. So what's the problem with Judaism? It's that our interpretation of the Bible seems different than anybody's interpretation.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.000
is the, what he calls the halakha, the Jewish law,

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.300
are the practice of Judaism,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.200
doesn't seem to jive with the Bible.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:48.840
All right?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.940
Now, again, we're talking about a society

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.500
which was highly educated.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.780
Ribbi David Nieto was the chief Ribbi of the Sepharadi community in England.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.360
and not only this is a very educated

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.000
society, but also

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.580
there was a psychological warfare going on.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.860
What was the psychological warfare? There were Jews in Portugal

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.960
and in Spain who attained extraordinary

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.100
achievements in literature and science

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.120
and commerce and we were trying to attract

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.180
them because they were still living, pretending

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.260
to be Christians in Spain. Some of these people

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:37.260
we were able to attract, and they came and they joined our communities. But these people, when they came to join our communities,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:47.260
all of a sudden, because they were alienated for 200, 300 years from Judaism, they seemed, they were uncomfortable. Yes.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:56.260
Alright? And therefore there was a need to explain the mechanism, yes, by which we interpret the Bible, we interpret everything.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:02.260
The thesis of this Hakham, which is my thesis, I defended this in many, in two of my books,

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:07.260
Ionim b'misheit r'al al-alambam, which is in Hebrew, I defended this thesis through halakha,

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:14.260
and another book which is in English is Golden Doves with Silver Darts, Textuality in Semitic and Rabbinic Liturgies.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:20.260
The thesis is the following. We have a Tora sheveh at bein. We have a tradition.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.260
Going back, I tell you the truth, I believe it is primo zayi, going to Abraham Rabbeinu.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:30.260
Yes? Of course the most authentic part is that that comes from Moshe Rabbenu, that comes from like the Milach.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:35.260
The Milach comes from Abel, the Achniso, Bibliotos of Abraham Rabbeinu.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:40.260
So there are ancient, very ancient traditions that goes even to Noah.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:47.260
I mean I believe that there is no society, that our society, the Sephardim, the Ashkenaz, the Jewish society in general,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.260
we are the recipients of the oldest tradition of civilized men.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:58.140
man. Could be even from Noah, could be even from pre-Noah, from Adam and Eishon. You know, that's my thesis.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:04.540
And we interpret what we interpret because of our tradition. Our tradition conditions

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:12.300
the way we look into the Bible. So in a sense, it is we interpret, we are what we are because of our

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:19.500
tradition. The Bible, we project our tradition in the Bible, you see. Now for instance, here is going to,

